@startuml class_global_simple
title Global class diagram --- essential structure

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor       #FFFFFF
  BorderColor           #6B2FA0
  BorderThickness       1.4
  HeaderBackgroundColor #6B2FA0
  FontColor             #FFFFFF
  FontName              Courier
  FontSize              14
  FontStyle             plain
  AttributeFontColor    #1A1A1A
  AttributeFontName     Courier
  AttributeFontSize     12
}
skinparam ArrowColor      #1A1A1A
skinparam ArrowThickness  1.4
skinparam ArrowFontColor  #4A5BBF
skinparam ArrowFontStyle  italic
skinparam ArrowFontName   Courier
skinparam ArrowFontSize   11
skinparam TitleFontName   Courier
skinparam TitleFontSize   16
skinparam TitleFontColor  #1A1A1A
skinparam noteBorderColor     #B9A0D4
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F6F1FB
skinparam noteFontName        Courier
skinparam noteFontSize        11
hide circle
hide members

class User
class Role
class Permission

class Project
class TeamAssignment

class WorkloadPlan
class ActualWorkload

class BillingMilestone
class Mission

class Sprint
class BacklogItem

class KpiSnapshot

' --- Access control: a role is data, not a subtype -------------------
User "*"  --> "1" Role       : holds >
Role "*"  --  "*" Permission : grants >

' --- The project is the aggregation root -----------------------------
Project "*" --> "1"    User : director >
Project "*" --> "0..1" User : project manager >

Project "1" *-- "*" TeamAssignment
TeamAssignment "*" --> "1" User : member >

Project "1" *-- "*" WorkloadPlan
Project "1" *-- "*" ActualWorkload
Project "1" *-- "*" BillingMilestone
Project "1" *-- "*" Mission
Project "1" *-- "*" Sprint
Project "1" *-- "*" BacklogItem
Project "1" *-- "*" KpiSnapshot

Sprint "0..1" o-- "*" BacklogItem : commits >

note right of Role
  The four roles are rows, not
  subclasses: the policy is data.
end note

note bottom of Project
  Governance registers are composed the same
  way and appear in their own diagram.
end note

@enduml
